> Bash cd /builds/looper/looper/issues/135; gh issue comment 135 --repo tacplus-dev/looper --body "Status of this run (it ends before the manager reached this land; the land stays queued and the manager lands it after me, the next run finishes the issue).  **Fix** (221a841, on looper/looper-135, queued for...
< https://github.com/tacplus-dev/looper/issues/135#issuecomment-6847979491 [2026-11-13T08:28:25Z] checkpoint of #135 (a step) pushed to looper/looper-135:  6 files changed, 424 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
The fix for #135 is committed (221a841) and queued for landing. It hasn't landed yet: the manager never reached it before this run's time ran out. So I haven't closed the issue; the manager lands it after this run and the next run finishes it.

**The fix:** in `looper-build`, the `status failure` path now ends its `sed` read of `build-verdict` with `|| true`. When the gates' child pipeline fails there is no verdict file, and before, `set -e` ended the script silently, so the status was never posted. Now it posts "the build failed".

**The test:** I added a case to `tests/looper-build.test.sh` for a failure with no verdict file. It failed before the fix and passes after it. Locally the whole file ends `looper-build: all passed`; only the docker reproducibility case was skipped, since there's no docker here.

**Not verified:**
- **The build job:** it ended `no verdict within 3h`, with the commit status stuck at `pending` since 05:08Z. The `build` gate set takes about 5 minutes, so this is most likely the same bug: the build image still runs main's `looper-build`, which can't report a red gates run. The pipeline is private, so I couldn't see whether the gates failed or why.
- **The land's gates:** they haven't run yet.

**Left for the next run:**
- When the manager posts its verdict, comment with the gate set it ran and close the issue.
- Add the issue's follow-up to PROPOSALS.md: put the gates job's verdict line in the status description. I didn't add it here because that would mean committing to the branch while it sits in the land queue.

I posted all of this on the issue and checkpointed the branch with the same notes for the next run.
